<title>USA: Technology Flavors Q3 loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Technology Flavors Q3 loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>AMITYVILLE, N.Y. 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Technology Flavors &amp; Fragrances Inc.</p>
<p>	     Three months ended Sept 30,   1996	     1995</p>
<p> Net sales				 $5,139,096	$4,075,979</p>
<p> Cost of sales			    3,172,693	 2,510,934</p>
<p> Gross profit			     1,966,403	 1,565,045</p>
<p>   Total operating expenses	   2,342,427	 1,488,660</p>
<p> Net income (loss)			(494,965)	    54,780</p>
<p> Net income (loss) per share		(.04)		.005</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p>   outstanding			   11,756,568	11,000,339</p>
<p>		Nine months ended Sept 30,   1996		1995</p>
<p> Net sales				$16,029,331     $11,960,168</p>
<p> Cost of sales			    9,754,345	 7,184,117</p>
<p> Gross profit			     6,274,986	 4,776,051</p>
<p>   Total operating expenses	   6,301,657	 4,520,537</p>
<p> Net income (loss)			(425,673)	   198,645</p>
<p> Net income (loss) per share		(.04)		 .02</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p>   outstanding			   11,756,568	11,174,062</p>
<p>NOTE: The company attributed the loss in part to the non-operating expenses arising from the 1995 Seafla buy.</p>
</text>
